# A <script> carrying an `@{ }` hole inside a region. internal/jsx's
# resolveMarkup walk lacked an *ast.MarkerRegion case, so ResolveScripts never
# classified the hole's JS context and emit rejected legitimate source with
# `error[unsafe-js-context]: <script> interpolation "v" has no JS context
# (internal error: ResolveScripts not run?)`. It failed CLOSED (no unsafe
# escaping), but the source is valid: the hole must lower to the same
# `_gsxgw.JSVal(v)` the <div> sibling produces.
-- input.gsx --
package views

component RegionScriptHole(v string) {
	<?start name="r">
		<script>const a = @{v};</script>
	<?end>
	<div>
		<script>const a = @{v};</script>
	</div>
}
-- invoke --
RegionScriptHole("</script>x")
